obs look: review 2 dashboard(s) in a browser

You are the reviewer. obs look has set the stack up and calls no LLM; the screenshots and the judgement are yours.

SANDBOX
  Grafana: http://127.0.0.1:3000 (anonymous viewer, nothing to log in to)
  seed window: 2026-11-17T09:30:00Z to 2026-11-17T10:00:00Z (the URLs fix it; do not change the time range)
  changed dashboards are those that differ from origin/main
  no incidents in this seed: Grafana's native state is current; no incident Firing state is expected.

STEPS
  1. For each dashboard below, open its URL in a browser with a viewport of 1600 x 1000 px.
     Wait until every panel has stopped loading (no spinners), then take a FULL-PAGE screenshot (the board is taller than the viewport)
     and save it at the given path. Keep the width at 1600 px.
  2. Open each screenshot and look at it. Judge it against EVERY checklist item: pass, fail or unclear.
     For a fail or unclear item, name the panel by title and say what you see. Do not judge from the JSON; judge from the image.
     If a panel needs a closer look, open its panel URL and save that shot too.
  3. Write ONE pull request comment for all dashboards, in the layout under COMMENT LAYOUT, with the images attached.
     If the pull request already has a comment that starts with <!-- obs-look -->, edit that one instead of adding a second.
     GitHub has no image-upload API: paste or drag each PNG into the comment box in the browser (GitHub uploads it and inserts the link),
     or upload it where the repo keeps assets and link it. If you cannot attach images, say so in the comment and give the file names.
  4. When done, `obs sandbox down --project demo --runtime docker` stops the stack (only the containers, volumes and network labelled obs.sandbox=demo).

DASHBOARDS
  1. Payments overview  (dashboards/overview.json)
     open: http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/payments-overview/payments-overview?orgId=1&from=1794907800000&to=1794909600000&var-ds=payments-metrics&var-outcome=error&var-provider=%24__all&var-route=%2Frefund&var-first=a&var-win=5m&kiosk
     save: obs-look/dashboards-overview.png
     variables set in the URL: $ds=payments-metrics (sandbox datasource); $outcome=error (first value on the seed); $provider=$__all (all values); $route=/refund (current); $first=a (first option); $win=5m (default)
     every other variable keeps Grafana's default; check that each populates and changes the view
     panels (open one only when the board shot is not enough):
       - panel 1 "Charges" (timeseries): http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/payments-overview/payments-overview?orgId=1&from=1794907800000&to=1794909600000&var-ds=payments-metrics&var-outcome=error&var-provider=%24__all&var-route=%2Frefund&var-first=a&var-win=5m&viewPanel=panel-1&kiosk -> obs-look/dashboards-overview-panel-1.png
       - panel 2 "Latency" (timeseries): http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/payments-overview/payments-overview?orgId=1&from=1794907800000&to=1794909600000&var-ds=payments-metrics&var-outcome=error&var-provider=%24__all&var-route=%2Frefund&var-first=a&var-win=5m&viewPanel=panel-2&kiosk -> obs-look/dashboards-overview-panel-2.png
       - panel 3 "Errors" (logs): http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/payments-overview/payments-overview?orgId=1&from=1794907800000&to=1794909600000&var-ds=payments-metrics&var-outcome=error&var-provider=%24__all&var-route=%2Frefund&var-first=a&var-win=5m&viewPanel=panel-3&kiosk -> obs-look/dashboards-overview-panel-3.png
  2. No uid  (dashboards/nouid.json)
     open: http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/obs-dashboards-nouid/no-uid?orgId=1&from=1794907800000&to=1794909600000&kiosk
     save: obs-look/dashboards-nouid.png

CHECKLIST (from docs/standards/grafana-dashboards/index.md)
  C1. No "No data" or error panels with synthetic data loaded
  C2. Units render as units (`1.2k req/s`, `250 ms`), not raw numbers
  C3. Legends readable and bounded; panel not swallowed by the legend
  C4. Every template variable populates and visibly changes the view

COMMENT LAYOUT
  <!-- obs-look -->
